// A program whose only dialect word is ui::WEB, the UI level it asks for:
// the auto-include serves <ns_ui_web> (the target that registers the level's
// host), and that fragment's own mentions of the dialect intrinsics
// (`println(stderr, ...)`) pull bits/std_format ahead of it. A fragment's
// unqualified mention reaches an intrinsic provider (bits/*); only a sibling
// namespace surface (ns_*) needs a qualified use (`madc::x`).
// Before the fix the program was refused: "ns_ui_web:117:6: use of
// undeclared identifier 'println'", unless the program itself happened to
// say print/println/format. So this program says none of them: its output is
// printf's. An IDE product's main unit (a madcide product built on the
// base) has the same shape: a descriptor naming ui::WEB, and no output of
// its own.
// Oracle: n/a for gcc/clang (the dialect's auto-include); the C analogue
// `long level = 3; printf(...)` prints the same line under gcc 13 and
// clang 18.
int main(void)
{
    long level = ui::WEB;
    printf("ui-web-alone: web-above-tui=%d\n", level > ui::TUI ? 1 : 0);
    return 0;
}
